    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Lead intake with expiring request keys\n\nThis workflow validates lead submissions and stores lead data separately from request-idempotency records. Active keys keep the existing replay behavior: the same normalized payload returns the original lead, while changed payloads return a conflict. Keys expire after 24 hours by default without deleting or changing their leads.\n\nNew requests still compare normalized email and non-empty phone values against stored leads. Possible person-level duplicates are inserted separately with `manual_review`, a matching lead ID, and the signals that matched. Name and company remain supporting signals only.\n\n### How it works\n\nThe webhook path hashes normalized business fields, checks only unexpired keys, inserts the lead, then stores a key record with its expiry. A scheduled path removes at most 100 expired key records each hour. Responses stay 202, 200, 409, or 400.\n\n### Setup\n\nImport the inactive workflow and complete the v0.3 migration in the README. Change `IDEMPOTENCY_TTL_HOURS` in **Validate and Normalize** if 24 hours is not suitable. Test every path before activation.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 1
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -560],
